       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Order as written:** ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum daily dose:** the usual limit for adults is 3,200 mg/day for inpatient or prescription use, so this is twice that.\n- **Maximum single dose:** the usual limit is 800 mg per dose, so 1600 mg in one dose is also too high.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day. This is the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is 1,600 mg/day. This is common for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy first."
